    <!-- ====================================================================
         Source: Catalogo_ATS.xls, sheet "TABLAS REFERENCIALES".
         Columns: B = Código, C = Tipo de Comprobante, D = Código Secuenciales
         Transacción, E = Fecha de vigencia (the literal 'vacío' in every row), F =
         Sustento tributario
         Rows 49 to 88, one record per row, in source order.
         Record ids are suffixed with the 1-based position in that order,
         so ats_catalog_entry_<table>_<n> is row 49 + n - 1.
         Every value below was read from the cell named above; nothing is
         interpolated.
    -->
    <!--
      * document_type_codes holds column F, the SRI's own "Sustento
        tributario" list: the Tabla 5 support types that apply to this
        document type. It is the other side of the same cross-reference
        Tabla 5 states in its own column, and the two do not fully
        agree. The literal 'ninguno' becomes an empty field.
      * column E reads 'vacío' in every row: the SRI publishes no validity
        date here, so date_start carries the sentinel, not a real date.
    -->
    <!--
      date_start 1900-01-01 is a SENTINEL, not a validity date. The sheet carries no
      date for this table (no date column, or the literal 'vacío' in every row) while
      the l10n.ec.temporal mixin makes date_start required. date_end stays empty so the
      entry reads as open-ended. See readme/ROADMAP.md for the open question.
    -->
